Z||000000||Haze_Performance||05-09-2000||03:52 PM||||I stoped to look at a Fiero "FOR SALE" last night in a gas station. It was black with a 14" silver stripe down the middle(Looked good) and the sunroof glass was etched to match the stripe.Well the guy came out and said that it was a 85 2M5 (Yes I said 2M5)I told him that it was a 2m4 but he said I was worng. Also the car had Formula and rear end with round moldings all around the car. In addition to his stupidity the car had Silver 16" Berretta GT wheels on it. He yelled at me saying the car was bone stock from the factory with all you see on it now.There wasnt a 85 Formula was there? I thought they came out in 87/88. Well anyway he wanted $2800. The car was a 4 speed with 120,000||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||05-09-2000||04:10 PM||||First, the only Formulas are 88's, Second, Only 84 4cyl's had 4spds 85 and 86 V-6's had 4spds also. Smooth molding was only on 86 and up GT's and 87/88 coupes/88 formula's. If it is an 85 somebody did a lot of swapping. $2800 seem a lot of money for it too! If it was in excellent condition I wouldn't go much over $1500 if that!||||reg||1
